  "corrected_reference_assumptions": [
    "The early harness incorrectly required a zero-byte physical file after ROLLBACK TO followed by RELEASE; pinned SQLite can retain an empty physical schema page. Logical catalog/rows/integrity equality remains required.",
    "The early corruption control treated a one-byte file as invalid. SQLite unixFileSize explicitly reports that length as zero (ticket #3260), even when the byte is nonzero. New positive cases cover bytes 0,65,255; invalid controls now start at two bytes. The old live audit also used a one-byte corruption fixture; it now uses two bytes. Logs retaining these failed assumptions and the failed first final live audit are included."
